 "text": "..title\nA resolution honoring the life and legacy of Grand Ole Opry announcer Bill Cody.\n\n..body\nWHEREAS, Nashville is known throughout the world as Music City, a place where songs, stories, and traditions are passed from one generation to the next; and\nWHEREAS, few individuals dedicated themselves more fully to preserving and sharing those traditions than Bill Cody, whose voice became synonymous with country music, the Grand Ole Opry, and the spirit of Nashville; and\nWHEREAS, for more than three decades, Bill Cody served as a trusted broadcaster, storyteller, interviewer, and ambassador for country music through his work with WSM Radio, the Grand Ole Opry, and the nationally recognized program Coffee, Country & Cody; and\nWHEREAS, through thousands of interviews and broadcasts, he welcomed legendary performers, rising stars, and devoted fans into conversations that celebrated both the rich history and evolving future of country music; and\nWHEREAS, Bill Cody possessed a rare gift for making every artist, listener, and guest feel valued, bringing warmth, authenticity, and genuine curiosity to every interaction, whether speaking with a Country Music Hall of Fame member or an aspiring songwriter making a first appearance in Music City; and\nWHEREAS, his extensive knowledge of country music history made him not only a broadcaster but also a historian and steward of one of America's most treasured art forms, helping preserve the stories behind the songs and the artists who shaped the genre; and\nWHEREAS, his contributions earned him widespread recognition throughout the broadcasting and music industries, including induction into the Country Radio Hall of Fame. However, his impact extended far beyond awards and accolades and is most obvious through the relationships he built and the lives he touched; and\nWHEREAS, generations of country music fans came to know Nashville through Bill Cody's voice, and generations of artists found in him a trusted friend, advocate, and champion of their work; and\nWHEREAS, throughout his career, Bill Cody embodied the values that have long defined the Grand Ole Opry and WSM Radio: respect for tradition, appreciation for artistry, commitment to excellence, and a deep love for the people who make country music possible; and\nWHEREAS, his passing on June 9, 2026, represents a profound loss not only for the country music community, but also for Nashville itself, a city whose story he helped tell each day through his words, his passion, and his unwavering dedication to the music and culture that define our community; and\nWHEREAS, while his voice may no longer echo across the airwaves, his influence will continue to be felt through the artists he encouraged, the listeners he inspired, and the enduring legacy he leaves within the Grand Ole Opry, WSM Radio, and Music City.\nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1. That the Metropolitan County Council hereby goes on record to honor the life and legacy of Bill Cody and recognize his enduring legacy with the Grand Ole Opry, WSM Radio, and Nashville and Davidson County.\nSection 2. This Resolution shall take effect from and after its adoption, the welfare of the Metropolitan Government requiring it.\n\n"
}
